      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "A new computerized method for analyzing biplane coronary arteriograms was proposed. The method extracted the vessels in an image, detected branching points, and identified vessel segments according to their anatomical names. The method was applied to a pair of orthogonal projection images acquired in the right anterior oblique and left anterior oblique views. It recognized the corresponding vessel segments in the images and labeled them correctly by their anatomical names. For diameter measurement, a combined first and second derivative filter process was applied to the images along the skeleton lines of the extracted vessel segments. We also designed a method of representation in which vessel diameters measured in the two projection images could be displayed in a single image."},
